A||||12||California Kid||SEAT BELT WARNING !!!||||4||
Z||000000||California Kid||07-31-2001||11:38 PM||||I have heard that there have been cases is some collisions where the belt will cut through the neck, servering arteries, and the person bleeds to death before reaching the hospital.<P>If your belt rides on your neck while your driving, you can probably understand why you should be concerned.<P>There is a real easy solution to prevent this from happening. Go to a Auto Parts Store and buy a cloth sleeve to wrap around the belt, they're very low cost and they come in many colors/fabric/materials. Pick a good one that will prevent the narrow edge of the nylon belt from coming into contact with your neck.<P>Think I did my good deed for the day, so I'm going to bed.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-01-2001||12:21 AM||||And make sure that the lap belt is on your hips, not in your stomach.<P>And that you wear it.<P>Even with an ejector seat.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||08-01-2001||08:10 AM||||A seat belt will not cut your neck in a collision. <P>If you were in an accident where that was a concern you would have more on your mind than a cut neck, most likely an engine.<P>The worst I've seen is a welt from where the belt rubbed on collision running from the collar area to the hip, no big deal.<P>Don't sweat it Kid. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||08-01-2001||08:15 AM||||External damage from a seat belt is like a floor burn, even through clothing...<BR>Corse, my lap belt fractured my pelvis in four places...<BR>crash...<p>[This message has been edited by Fierowrecker (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
