Z||000006||rogergarrison||08-01-2001||02:31 PM||||A girl I know flipped her Saturn 3 times after hitting the side of a semi. she got some really nasty cuts on her shoulders and neck from seatbelt. bruised from her boob to her ear. But she was able to walk away.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierohoho||08-01-2001||03:35 PM||||Roger, knowing how many small items women keep in the car(no offense ladies <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)and the fact she rolled it 3 times, could she have been cut by stuff like flying glass or flying objects in the car?<P>Not to say it's impossible to be cut by the seatbelt, I'm sure the body moves around quite a bit on the flip flop and could slide back and forth along the belt.<P>Just an observation not meant to cause a problem.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
