Z||000010||California Kid||08-01-2001||11:37 PM||||My post on this item was intended to give all of you a little "heads up" and make your own decisions. The information was gotten from "inside sources" within the Big 3 that deal with seat belts.  I won't get specific because I don't want to lose my job over this. Not trying to scare anyone or promote products, the choice is yours!!!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Rob Durham||08-02-2001||10:02 AM||||I am with the rescue team at the Sherrif's Dept. and we were called to an accident one evening involving 2 cars and a semi one of the drivers was wearing his seatbelt but had it up under his arm instead of over his shoulder and it cut him all the way up into the bottom of his socket, so yes seatbelts CAN cut you!<P>I have also seen death caused by seatbelts although for the most part you are safer wearing them!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://rs-designs.com/87GT.html" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://rs-designs.com/Banner.jpg">   </A><p>[This message has been edited by Rob Durham (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||11
